    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0616" n="596" xml:id="pg596"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 18th instant, in relation to the case of Mr. James
                    McHugh, and to inform your lordship, in reply, that on the 11th instant I called
                    upon General Dix for information as to the progress of the investigation in this
                    case, since which I have had no advices on the subject. I have now requested the
                    Secretary of War to require such information from the proper authorities, and
                    have laid before him a copy of your note.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
